Session 21 (sess39) closed 5 defects and found 3, net 9 → 7 OPEN, across builds 0.11.326→330 with **five consecutive all-green 22-test boards** (322, 325, 326, 327, 330):

**Fixed and verified (4):**
- **Wire-EX slot leak, both mechanisms.** The 13.4K orphaned lock slots were traced to two evict-time holes: the sess37 retention branch trusting in-memory mode while the wire held EX (326 fix: wire-confirmed-PR retention), and — the dominant one, dlmtr-traced to the exact line — the deferred-publish evict skip assuming "unpublished ⇒ no on-disk slot" while every created file's slot actually exists (330 fix: wire-truth read at the skip). Bulk verification went from 190-200 leaked slots per batch to 0.
- **Release barrier**: cluster-wide census after a full board showed ~130K wire unlocks with zero open obligations on all 32 nodes; disposed per its own ledgered test.
- **statfs drift** (n1 reporting −10851 inodes used): architectural — percpu counters only see local deltas; fixed per GPT-reviewed design with cluster-coherent per-AG sums plus mount-time AG init. Cross-node agreement verified; admission counters deliberately untouched (the near-ENOSPC overcommit question is recorded as a follow-up thread).

**Disproved (2):** the dir_reuse "bimodality" is deterministic run-over-run degradation caused by the host rig's storage path (pure-host fsync probe degrades p90 26→95ms during plateau runs, below the entire mxfs stack; recovers with ~25min idle — rig rule recorded); the "pinned inode" defect was upstream page-cache LRU design plus a slab-only drop_caches repro artifact.

**Also landed:** `dir_ex_batch_grace_ms` default 40→10 (turn p50 81→50ms, first-ever consecutive 9-round dir_reuse), and the misguided 329 sweep neutralized to opt-in.

Remaining OPEN: the authority family (3, AGI canary quiet through five boards' crash cycles), two pace defects awaiting re-baseline under the fresh-storage rig rule, the dirview non-convergence, and the rig-blocked matrix columns. All state is in the ledger, CHANGELOG, and four ccmemory entries; the relay continues from the authority family and pace re-baseline.

